{"version":"6.9","hitCount":765,"nextCursorMark":"AoIIQEDvEig0ODE2NTgwNg==","nextPageUrl":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=%28TITLE%3A%22protein+structure+prediction%22+OR+ABSTRACT%3A%28alphafold%29%29+AND+LANG%3Aeng+AND+HAS_ABSTRACT%3AY+AND+%28NOT+PUB_TYPE%3A%22Retracted+Publication%22%29+AND+%28NOT+TITLE%3A%28review%29%29+AND+PUB_YEAR%3A%5B2021+TO+2023%5D&cursorMark=AoIIQEDvEig0ODE2NTgwNg%3D%3D&resultType=core&pageSize=3&format=json","request":{"queryString":"(TITLE:\"protein structure prediction\" OR ABSTRACT:(alphafold)) AND LANG:eng AND HAS_ABSTRACT:Y AND (NOT PUB_TYPE:\"Retracted Publication\") AND (NOT TITLE:(review)) AND PUB_YEAR:[2021 TO 2023]","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":3,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"37060758","source":"MED","pmid":"37060758","doi":"10.1016/j.sbi.2023.102594","title":"Progress at protein structure prediction, as seen in CASP15.","authorString":"Elofsson A.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Elofsson A","lastName":"Elofsson","firstName":"Arne","initials":"A","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7115-9751"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Science for Life Laboratory and Dep. of Biochemistry and Biophysics, Stockholm University, Sweden. Electronic address: arne@bioinfo.se."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7115-9751"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics"]},"journalInfo":{"volume":"80","journalIssueId":3581609,"dateOfPublication":"2023 Jun","monthOfPublication":6,"yearOfPublication":2023,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Curr Opin Struct Biol","title":"Current opinion in structural biology","essn":"1879-033X","issn":"0959-440X","nlmid":"9107784","isoabbreviation":"Curr Opin Struct Biol"},"printPublicationDate":"2023-06-01"},"pubYear":"2023","pageInfo":"102594","abstractText":"In Dec 2020, the results of AlphaFold version 2 were presented at CASP14, sparking a revolution in the field of protein structure predictions. For the first time, a purely computational method could challenge experimental accuracy for structure prediction of single protein domains. The code of AlphaFold v2 was released in the summer of 2021, and since then, it has been shown that it can be used to accurately predict the structure of most ordered proteins and many protein-protein interactions. It has also sparked an explosion of development in the field, improving AI-based methods to predict protein complexes, disordered regions, and protein design. Here I will review some of the inventions sparked by the release of AlphaFold.","affiliation":"Science for Life Laboratory and Dep. of Biochemistry and Biophysics, Stockholm University, Sweden. Electronic address: arne@bioinfo.se.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Review","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Knut och Alice Wallenbergs Stiftelse","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Vetenskapsrådet","grantId":"2021-03979","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Linköpings Universitet","grantId":"SNIC 2021/5-297","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Protein Conformation"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Protein Domains"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.sbi.2023.102594"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":83,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"Y","hasData":"N","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2023-06-05","dateOfCreation":"2023-04-15","dateOfRevision":"2023-06-19","electronicPublicationDate":"2023-04-14","firstPublicationDate":"2023-04-14","firstIndexDate":"2023-04-16","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"37565699","source":"MED","pmid":"37565699","doi":"10.1002/prot.26570","title":"Improved protein structure prediction with trRosettaX2, AlphaFold2, and optimized MSAs in CASP15.","authorString":"Peng Z, Wang W, Wei H, Li X, Yang J.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Peng Z","lastName":"Peng","firstName":"Zhenling","initials":"Z","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"MOE Frontiers Science Center for Nonlinear Expectations, Research Center for Mathematics and Interdisciplinary Sciences, Shandong University, Qingdao, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang W","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Wenkai","initials":"W","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8603-8250"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Mathematical Sciences, Nankai University, Tianjin, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wei H","lastName":"Wei","firstName":"Hong","initials":"H","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"School of Mathematical Sciences, Nankai University, Tianjin, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Li X","lastName":"Li","firstName":"Xiaoge","initials":"X","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"MOE Frontiers Science Center for Nonlinear Expectations, Research Center for Mathematics and Interdisciplinary Sciences, Shandong University, Qingdao, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Yang J","lastName":"Yang","firstName":"Jianyi","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"MOE Frontiers Science Center for Nonlinear Expectations, Research Center for Mathematics and Interdisciplinary Sciences, Shandong University, Qingdao, China."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8603-8250"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"12","volume":"91","journalIssueId":3667952,"dateOfPublication":"2023 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":2023,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Proteins","title":"Proteins","essn":"1097-0134","issn":"0887-3585","nlmid":"8700181","isoabbreviation":"Proteins"},"printPublicationDate":"2023-12-01"},"pubYear":"2023","pageInfo":"1704-1711","abstractText":"We present the monomer and multimer structure prediction results of our methods in CASP15. We first designed an elaborate pipeline that leverages complementary sequence databases and advanced database searching algorithms to generate high-quality multiple sequence alignments (MSAs). Top MSAs were then selected for the subsequent step of structure prediction. We utilized trRosettaX2 and AlphaFold2 for monomer structure prediction (group name Yang-Server), and AlphaFold-Multimer for multimer structure prediction (group name Yang-Multimer). Yang-Server and Yang-Multimer are ranked at the top and the fourth, respectively, for monomer and multimer structure prediction. For 94 monomers, the average TM-score of the predicted structure models by Yang-Server is 0.876, compared to 0.798 by the default AlphaFold2 (i.e., the group NBIS-AF2-standard). For 42 multimers, the average DockQ score of the predicted structure models by Yang-Multimer is 0.464, compared to 0.389 by the default AlphaFold-Multimer (i.e., the group NBIS-AF2-multimer). Detailed analysis of the results shows that several factors contribute to the improvement, including improved MSAs, iterated modeling for large targets, interplay between monomer and multimer structure prediction for intertwined structures, etc. However, the structure predictions for orphan proteins and multimers remain challenging, and breakthroughs in this area are anticipated in the future.","affiliation":"MOE Frontiers Science Center for Nonlinear Expectations, Research Center for Mathematics and Interdisciplinary Sciences, Shandong University, Qingdao, China.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grantId":"T2222012","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grantId":"T2225007","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Furylfuramide"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Sequence Alignment"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Algorithms"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Databases, Nucleic Acid"}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Multiple sequence alignment","Protein Structure Prediction","Alphafold2","Multimer Structure Prediction","Trrosetta"]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Furylfuramide","registryNumber":"054NR2135Y"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/prot.26570"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":34,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2023-11-24","dateOfCreation":"2023-08-11","dateOfRevision":"2025-09-30","electronicPublicationDate":"2023-08-10","firstPublicationDate":"2023-08-10","firstIndexDate":"2023-08-14","hasEvaluations":"N"},{"id":"37018272","source":"MED","pmid":"37018272","doi":"10.1109/tcbb.2022.3233846","title":"TemPred: A Novel Protein Template Search Engine to Improve Protein Structure Prediction.","authorString":"Tripathi A, Mondal R, Lahiri T, Chaurasiya D, Pal MK.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Tripathi A","lastName":"Tripathi","firstName":"Asmita","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Mondal R","lastName":"Mondal","firstName":"Rajkrishna","initials":"R","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5557-371X"}},{"fullName":"Lahiri T","lastName":"Lahiri","firstName":"Tapobrata","initials":"T","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0290-4201"}},{"fullName":"Chaurasiya D","lastName":"Chaurasiya","firstName":"Deepak","initials":"D","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0002-2722-9043"}},{"fullName":"Pal MK","lastName":"Pal","firstName":"Manoj Kumar","initials":"MK"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5557-371X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0290-4201"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0002-2722-9043"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"20","journalIssueId":3582900,"dateOfPublication":"2023 May-Jun","monthOfPublication":0,"yearOfPublication":2023,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"IEEE/ACM Trans Comput Biol Bioinform","title":"IEEE/ACM transactions on computational biology and bioinformatics","essn":"1557-9964","issn":"1545-5963","nlmid":"101196755","isoabbreviation":"IEEE/ACM Trans Comput Biol Bioinform"},"printPublicationDate":"2023-05-01"},"pubYear":"2023","pageInfo":"2112-2121","abstractText":"Among new protein structure predictors, the recently developed AlphaFold predictor relies on contact map in line with contact map potential based threading model that basically relies on fold recognition. In parallel, sequence similarity based homology model relies on homologue recognition. Both of these methods rely on sequence-structure or sequence-sequence similarity with protein with known structure in absence of which, as argued in the development of AlphaFold, the structure prediction becomes quite challenging. However, the term, \"known structure\" depends on the similarity method adopted to identify it, for example, through sequence match yielding homologue or sequence-structure match yielding a fold. Also, quite often, AlphaFold structures are found to be not acceptable by the structure evaluating gold standard parameters. In this context, this work utilized the concept of ordered local physicochemical property, ProtPCV by Pal et al (2020) providing a new similarity criteria to identify the template protein with known structure. Finally a template search engine, TemPred was developed using the ProtPCV similarity criteria. It was intriguing to find that quite often templates generated by TemPred were better than that produced by the conventional search engines. It pointed out the need of combined approach to get better structural model for a protein.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Proteins","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Algorithms"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Models, Molecular"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Software"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Search Engine"}]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"Proteins","registryNumber":"0"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TCBB.2022.3233846"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","citedByCount":3,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"N","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"N","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"N","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCompletion":"2023-06-07","dateOfCreation":"2023-04-05","dateOfRevision":"2023-06-07","electronicPublicationDate":"2023-06-05","firstPublicationDate":"2023-05-01","firstIndexDate":"2023-04-06","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}